From: Celestials316 <210317976+Celestials316@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 22:10:12 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] deps,ngtcp2: keep sfparse out of the libnode link
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

deps/nghttp2/nghttp2.gyp compiles lib/sfparse.c into libnghttp2.a (the
HTTP/2 stack itself calls it), while deps/ngtcp2/ngtcp2.gyp builds a
second, separate sfparse static library for its ngtcp2_test_server /
ngtcp2_test_client example targets. Those examples are disabled
(type:none) while they await C++23, but gyp still collects the archives
of a target's entire dependency closure onto the link line of every
dependent, and node.gypi lists both example targets as libnode
dependencies when QUIC is enabled with the bundled OpenSSL. The Android
shared libnode therefore links libnghttp2.a and libsfparse.a side by
side, and ld.lld refuses every duplicate sfparse_* symbol
("ld.lld: error: duplicate symbol: sfparse_parser_dict").

Drop the dangling dependency: the disabled examples compile nothing and
lose nothing, nghttp3's sfparse_* references resolve against the copy
inside libnghttp2.a, and the duplicate disappears from the link.

---
 deps/ngtcp2/ngtcp2.gyp | 2 --
 1 file changed, 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/deps/ngtcp2/ngtcp2.gyp b/deps/ngtcp2/ngtcp2.gyp
index 7ae6279248..3fa446313b 100644
--- a/deps/ngtcp2/ngtcp2.gyp
+++ b/deps/ngtcp2/ngtcp2.gyp
@@ -267,7 +267,6 @@
         'ngtcp2',
         'nghttp3',
         '../openssl/openssl.gyp:openssl',
-        '../nghttp2/nghttp2.gyp:sfparse',
       ],
       'defines': [
         'HAVE_CONFIG_H',
@@ -328,7 +327,6 @@
         'ngtcp2',
         'nghttp3',
         '../openssl/openssl.gyp:openssl',
-        '../nghttp2/nghttp2.gyp:sfparse',
       ],
       'defines': [
         'HAVE_CONFIG_H',
